ri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Triacylglycerols</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="260" name="Google Shape;260;p35"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="762000"/><a:ext cx="8229600" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="This is a comparison of the structures of glycerol and trialcylglycerol, with Kekule structures and ball models.&#xA;At the top of the diagram is a Kekule structure of glycerol, shaded orange. Glycerol's carbons are numbered beginning on the left. C1 is part of CH2, which bonds down and left to OH, and down and right to C2, which is part of CH. CH bonds down to OH and right and up to C3, which is part of CH2, and bonds down and right to OH. Below is a ball model of triacylglycerol, shown as two long, charcoal gray carbon chains with a curved carbon chain in the middle. They converge at the top where there are 2 red atoms that represent oxygen. Below is the Kekule structure of triacylglycerol. The glycerol chain, shaded orange, is the central portion. C1 bonds left to O, which bonds left to C, which double bonds up and left to O and down to a long carbon chain. C2 bonds down to O, which bonds down to C, which double bonds up and left to O, and down to a long carbon chain which has 2 cis-configured double bonds and curves to the right. On the right, C3 bonds down and right to O, which bonds right to C, which double bonds up and right to O and down and right to a long carbon chain. The text at the bottom reads, &quot;1-Stearoyl, 2-linoleoyl, 3-palmitoyl glycerol, a mixed triacylglycerol.&quot;" id="261" name="Google Shape;261;p35"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="1889125" y="1011237"/><a:ext cx="5197475" cy="5684837"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>